<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! cold-boot-ceremony — Contract

Void-start identity builder. Runs on first boot when `IdentitiesDoc` has no principals.

Given a hex-encoded 32-byte Ed25519 verifying key, derives `did:key` (multicodec `0xed01` + base58btc, UCAN/Keyhive aligned) and returns two tiddler records:

* `IdentityTiddler` titled `@identities/{did}` — the per-vessel device leaf, `kind = "device"`, `verifyingKey` populated for Keyhive upgrade
* `CircleTiddler` titled `@circles/operators` — sole-member operators group, `capabilityPolicy = "group:operators"`

''Those titles name NAMESPACES, never bags.'' A title resolves verbatim inside its own document, so both spell the same in every face's planes and one internal shape serves them all. The BAGS answering to them carry the face's tag — `@identities-<tag>`, `@circles-<tag>`, derived off the PersonaGroup's own doc id — because a face's relations travel with the FACE, and a vessel-global bag would seat one persona's records beside another's where anything reading it correlates the faces a multitude exists to hold apart.

The device Ed25519 keypair roots the DEVICE; the operator identity rides the PersonaGroup root that delegates to it. GitHub / BlueSky auth enriches `displayName` only.

Caller MUST check the identity tiddler does not already exist before writing (idempotent guard).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

